{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/664022-favorite-pulp-game","id":664022,"title":"Favorite Pulp Game?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-14T00:20:38-07:00","id":664022,"title":"Favorite Pulp Game?","content":"I've been reading Hollow Earth Expedition and really enjoying it. I'm torn though on the mechanics, because Adventure! of course did one of the best jobs capturing pulp themes directly into character mechanics I've seen. So now I'm leaning toward running the Hollow Earth Expedition setting with Adventure! mechanics. I will need to come up with mechanics for Sorcery, the Atlantean Language, Beastmen and Martians if I do though.<br /> <br /> Any suggestions? Thoughts? Should I give HEX a chance as written?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T10:00:29-07:00","id":664513,"title":"","content":"Eh, I've always favored Spirit of the Century for the more pulpy games... on the flip side Savage Worlds by default strives for the pulp feel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T00:09:11-07:00","id":665427,"title":"","content":"Great. Now I gotta go bug Telgar and ask him what that pulpy Star Trek meets Flash Gordon sci-fi game he was waving at me is called. It was cool. I'll update.<br /> <br /> Update: Totally remembered all by myself, like a big boy.<br /> <br /> Cosmic Patrol.<br /> <br /> Pulpy, classic style rayguns, alien mining planets, rockets, ACTION and a VERY story oriented system. The mechanics are pretty flexible, so you can do a LOT with them if you fiddle with stuff. Already has a few species and archetypes statted, along with mechanics for weird powers, so that might help if you feel like reskinning some. It uses multiple kinds of dice; d4, d6, d8 and I think two more, probably a d10 and d20 iirc. That might be a tiny annoyance, but with online rollers or a varied dice collection, you're fine. You won't be rolling a lot.<br /> <br /> It makes me think of a weird Star Trek edition of Adventure! in how it treats your story. I'm so glad OPP acquired the rights to Adventure!. A new release would be awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":380,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","user":"AzraelFirestorm","date":". 09-15-2015, 03:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T13:39:43-07:00","id":666042,"title":"","content":"If we're leaving out <i>Adventure!</i>, then definitely <i>Spirit of the Century</i>. And <i>Hollow Earth Expeditions</i> is also excellent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T14:05:37-07:00","id":666059,"title":"","content":"As I said before, I'm tempted to play HEX using Adventure! mechanics. I love how HEX fleshed out some of the pulpy settings that other games like Adventure! and Spirit largely glaze over, but I'm partial to Adventure!'s character system and dramatic editing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}